#      that was true when written. The rule: a narrow-layer workaround is DEBT
#      until removed; fixing the root does not retire it, it makes it run twice.
#      Needed as a seed because nothing else sees it: duplication fails no build,
#      changes no exit code, and reddens no substring-anchored seed.
